{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-99313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ what are the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors of $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6de7d72e6a4b9ce87ad8ea9dbaa64046422b261e8"} {"question" "q-99313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\n- From the matrix $C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -(-1) & -2\\end{aligned}],$ we deduce that $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=-2$ and $\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=-1.$ So, our eigenvalue is\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2+(-1)\\text{i}=-2-\\text{i}.\n$$\n\n- From the matrix $P=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}],$ we deduce that our corresponding eigenvector is\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}3+0\\text{i} \\\\ 5+(-2)\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda ,$ and the second eigenvector must be the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nTherefore, our eigenvalues and eigenvectors are \n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2∓\\text{i},\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5∓2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6de7d72e6a4b9ce87ad8ea9dbaa64046422b261e8"} {"question" "q-99313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7166ee5fdb9a55a873b7fd8244d7357cc9a484e35e7df5db86fc0dfeea5b7d52"} {"question" "q-99313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6de7d72e6a4b9ce87ad8ea9dbaa64046422b261e8"} {"question" "q-99313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\lambda =-2∓\\text{i}$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2∓5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =-2∓\\text{i}$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5∓2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =1∓2\\text{i}$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1∓2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =1∓2\\text{i}$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5∓2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$\\lambda =5∓2\\text{i}$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2∓\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6de7d72e6a4b9ce87ad8ea9dbaa64046422b261e8"} {"question" "q-99313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\lambda =-2∓\\text{i}$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5∓2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6de7d72e6a4b9ce87ad8ea9dbaa64046422b261e8"} {"question" "q-39130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ what are the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors of $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6de7d72e6a4b9ce87ad8ea9dbaa64046422b261e8"} {"question" "q-39130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\n- From the matrix $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -(-2) & 5\\end{aligned}],$ we deduce that $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=5$ and $\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=-2.$ So, our eigenvalue is\n\n$$\n\\lambda =5+(-2)\\text{i}=5-2\\text{i}.\n$$\n\n- From the matrix $P=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ we deduce that our corresponding eigenvector is\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-1+4\\text{i} \\\\ 3+0\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1+4\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda ,$ and the second eigenvector must be the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nTherefore, our eigenvalues and eigenvectors are \n\n$$\n\\lambda =5∓2\\text{i},\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}-1\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6de7d72e6a4b9ce87ad8ea9dbaa64046422b261e8"} {"question" "q-39130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7166ee5fdb9a55a873b7fd8244d7357cc9a484e35e7df5db86fc0dfeea5b7d52"} {"question" "q-39130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6de7d72e6a4b9ce87ad8ea9dbaa64046422b261e8"} {"question" "q-39130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\lambda =5\\mp 2\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}-1\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6de7d72e6a4b9ce87ad8ea9dbaa64046422b261e8"} {"question" "q-99329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ what are the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors of $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6de7d72e6a4b9ce87ad8ea9dbaa64046422b261e8"} {"question" "q-99329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\n- From the matrix $C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -(-2) & 0\\end{aligned}],$ we deduce that $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0$ and $\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=-2.$ So, our eigenvalue is\n\n$$\n\\lambda =0+(-2)\\text{i}=-2\\text{i}.\n$$\n\n- From the matrix $P=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ we deduce that our corresponding eigenvector is\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}4+1\\text{i} \\\\ -3+(-1)\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+\\text{i} \\\\ -3-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda ,$ and the second eigenvector must be the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nTherefore, our eigenvalues and eigenvectors are \n\n$$\n\\lambda =∓2\\text{i},\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}4\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ -3∓\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6de7d72e6a4b9ce87ad8ea9dbaa64046422b261e8"} {"question" "q-99329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7166ee5fdb9a55a873b7fd8244d7357cc9a484e35e7df5db86fc0dfeea5b7d52"} {"question" "q-99329" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071601/state.json" "file_sha256" "810646eb602bf82225fb1fc6